  "Frame 5 (training doll, A1): in 'down' the grandmother's lips cover the doll's mouth and nose; the head is level; the chest rise is a small drawn lift plus the player's light patch. The doll has moulded closed eyes and no cap or wrap (the rest of the set shows a capped, wrapped newborn).",
  "Frame 2 (training doll, C5): the mother (teal dress) rubs the doll's back with a dry towel; the doll lies on its side, face turned to the side on a folded towel, nose and mouth at the towel's edge. The line says 'rub the back or the soles' (s4) and 'rub the back gently' (s1). In s1 and s2 the grandmother does the drying; here it is the mother.",
  "Frame 6 (10 Oct): the baby's face in profile with the nose and mouth free; a faint closed-eye line is drawn."
 ]
